.TH CCODE-CLI 1 "September 2026" "ccode v0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccode-cli \- terminal AI coding assistant (CLI backend)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccode-cli
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROMPT\fR | \fB\-i\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccode-cli
is a lightweight local coding agent speaking the OpenAI-compatible Chat
Completions API (streaming SSE). It runs in one of three modes:
.TP
.B Single prompt
.BI \-p " PROMPT"
sends one prompt and exits.
.TP
.B Interactive REPL
.BI \-i
reads prompts from stdin until EOF or
.BR /exit .
.TP
.B JSON Lines protocol
.BI \-\-json
speaks a line-based JSON protocol on stdin/stdout; this is what the
.BR ccode-tui (1)
frontend uses to drive it (and what the single
.BR ccode (1)
binary used in-process), and it can be reused by other frontends.
.PP
NOTE (September 2026, temporary): only
.B ccode-cli
is built;
.BR ccode (1)
and
.BR ccode-tui (1)
are paused but documented for reference.
.PP
The agent can inspect and modify the workspace with tools; by default
only read-only tools are enabled, pass
.B \-\-write
to enable write tools. Read-only tools, web_fetch/web_search, task and
agent_tool run without confirmation; edit_file/move_file and bash run
without confirmation only while every path they touch stays inside the
workspace. delete_file and any call that may leave the workspace always
prompt.
.PP
Dangerous bash commands are classified before approval: credential or
elevated commands require typing
.BR Yes ;
power/resource-destroying commands require typing
.BR \&Yes,\ do\ as\ I\ say. ;
raw-device, filesystem, partition and boot changes are refused and the
model is told to hand them to the user; commands that would destroy the
running system are refused outright. The typed confirmations are not
bypassed by
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-prompt " TEXT"
Send one prompt then exit. Ignored when
.B \-i
is also given.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Read prompts from stdin until EOF or
.BR /exit .
When stdin is a terminal, the input line is edited in raw mode with
readline-style keys (arrows, Home/End/Delete, Ctrl-A/E/K/U/W); Up/Down
walk back and forth through the prompts entered this session.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Use the JSON Lines protocol (machine mode). Implies interactive.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Accepted for option compatibility with
.BR ccode (1);
.B ccode-cli
itself stays in CLI/REPL mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " PATH"
Accepted; only the
.BR ccode-tui (1)
frontend uses it to locate its backend (see
.BR ccode-tui (1)
for the lookup order).
.TP
.B \-\-no-tui
Accepted; no effect on
.BR ccode-cli .
(It is an escape hatch for the
.B ccode
single binary on Windows consoles.)
.TP
.BI \-\-api-base " URL"
OpenAI-compatible API base URL (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_BASE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-api-key " KEY"
API key (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_KEY ;
see
.B CCODE_API_KEY_FILE
for the file-based variant).
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name (defaults to
.BR CCODE_MODEL ).
.TP
.B \-\-write
Enable the editor's str_replace command, bash, and the remaining
write-capable tools.
.TP
.B \-\-read-only
Read-only tools (editor view, glob, grep, read_tool_output). The default.
.TP
.B \-\-minimal
Minimal mode in the spirit of deepseek-harness's \fBminimal\fR agent
preset: a fixed one-sentence system prompt and exactly two tools,
str_replace_editor and bash. Per-turn change-log/task summaries are not
injected into the conversation. Implies
.BR \-\-write .
.TP
.B \-\-default
Fast start: interactive REPL plus read/write tools plus thinking
at
.BR high " effort."
Never enables
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Same as
.B \-\-default
but also print each provider tool call as raw OpenAI response JSON
.RB ( "[tool-call] " )
on stderr. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-auto-approve
Approve all remaining tool requests without prompting (also
.BR CCODE_AUTO_APPROVE=1 ).
Dangerous bash commands still require their typed confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-allowdanger
DANGER: disable every tool-call security check \em sensitive-path and
destructive-command filters, the Landlock write sandbox, and the web_fetch
host blacklist / private-network (SSRF) gate \em and imply
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
Only for trusted or throwaway environments; a warning is printed at startup.
.TP
.B \-\-thinking
Send the
.B "thinking"
field
.RB ( type:
.BR enabled ).
On by default; disable with
.BR CCODE_THINKING=0
or the
.B /thinking off
REPL command. Independent of
.BR \-\-reasoning .
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning
Send the reasoning_effort field (default effort:
.BR high ).
Independent of
.BR \-\-thinking .
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-effort " LEVEL"
Reasoning effort:
.BR low ", " medium ", " high ", " xhigh
or
.BR max .
Implies reasoning on.
.TP
.BI \-\-thinking-effort " LEVEL"
Alias for
.BR \-\-reasoning-effort .
.TP
.B \-\-allow-http
Allow
.BR http://
API endpoints beyond loopback (also
.BR CCODE_ALLOW_HTTP=1 ).
Plaintext traffic, known risk. Loopback http is always allowed;
remote http is refused otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-no-markdown
Disable markdown rendering in human-facing output.
.TP
.BI \-\-context-tokens " N"
Approximate context window in tokens; the conversation is compacted when the
estimated request reaches 90% of it. Default 1000000 (DeepSeek family);
0 disables the token trigger. The estimate is char-based (no tokenizer).
.TP
.BI \-\-max-turns " N"
Maximum assistant turns the agent loop may run for one prompt. Default 50;
0 means no limit. Sub-agents inherit the parent's value. When the cap is
reached the loop stops and prints a
.B [turn limit]
notice to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-save-session " PATH"
Save the conversation to
.I PATH
after each prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " PATH"
Load a conversation from
.I PATH
before the run.
.TP
.BI \-\-session-dir " DIR"
Session storage directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.SH REPL SLASH COMMANDS
.TP
.B /help
Show available commands.
.TP
.B /exit
Quit the REPL.
.TP
.B /quit
Alias for
.BR /exit .
.TP
.B /clear
Forget in-conversation history for this session.
.TP
.B /compact
Compact the conversation history (folds old messages into summaries).
.TP
.B /history
Print prompts entered this session.
.TP
.B /model [NAME]
Show the current model or switch to
.IR NAME .
.TP
.B /model default NAME
Persist the default model.
.TP
.B /models
List available models from the API.
.TP
.B /models search KEYWORD
Search models.
.TP
.B /models info NAME
Show model details.
.TP
.B /thinking [on|off]
Show or toggle the thinking field.
.TP
.B /reasoning [on|off]
Show or toggle the reasoning_effort field.
.TP
.B /reasoning effort LEVEL
Set reasoning effort (low, medium, high, xhigh, max).
.TP
.B /thinking effort LEVEL
Legacy alias for
.B /reasoning effort.
.TP
.B /sessions
List saved sessions. Aliases:
.B /session list
and
.BR "/resume \-\-list" .
.TP
.B /sessions delete NAME
Delete a session file.
.TP
.B /sessions rename OLD NEW
Rename a session file.
.TP
.B /sessions export NAME FORMAT
Export a session (json, md, txt).
.TP
.B /resume [NAME]
Resume a session (most recent if no name).
.TP
.B /session new [NAME]
Start a new session (optionally saved as NAME; a given NAME must end in
.IR .json ,
contain no slash, and fit the session-name length limit).
.TP
.B /session switch NAME
Switch to a saved session.
.SH TOOLS
.PP
Read-only (always available):
read_file, glob, grep, read_tool_output.
.PP
read_tool_output returns a window of an oversized tool result that was
archived under the session's results directory (the inline result was
truncated). Pass the tool_call_id of the truncated result; stream selects
stdout (default) or stderr for commands; offset and limit are optional
(limit capped at 64 KiB per call).
.PP
Read-write (with
.BR \-\-write ):
edit_file (empty old_string creates; refuses overwrite),
delete_file, move_file, bash,
web_fetch, web_search, agent_tool, task (action=create/update/list).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.SS API
.TP
.B CCODE_API_BASE
API base URL (required).
.TP
.B CCODE_API_KEY
API key (required).
.TP
.B CCODE_API_KEY_FILE
Path to a key file (regular file, single hard link, mode 0600).
.TP
.B CCODE_MODEL
Default model name (required).
.TP
.B CCODE_MODEL_VERIFY
Set 1 to check the configured model against the API model list before
the first request.
.TP
.B CCODE_MODEL_FALLBACK
Fallback model used only when verification confirms the configured
model is absent (a verification failure caused by a network error
leaves the model unchanged).
.TP
.B CCODE_WORKSPACE
Workspace directory (default: current directory).
.SS Tools and security
.TP
.B CCODE_READ_ONLY_TOOLS
Set 1 to enable read-only tools (already the default).
.TP
.B CCODE_WRITE_TOOLS
Set 1 to enable write tools (same as
.BR \-\-write ).
.TP
.B CCODE_MINIMAL
Set 1 for minimal mode (same as
.BR \-\-minimal ).
.TP
.B CCODE_AUTO_APPROVE
Set 1 to skip interactive approval.
.TP
.B CCODE_DISABLE_COMMAND_FILTER
Set 1 to disable sensitive-path and destructive-command filtering
(not recommended).
.TP
.B CCODE_RESPECT_GITIGNORE
Set 1 to have glob/grep honor .gitignore.
.SS Networking and TLS
.TP
.B CCODE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT
Overall request timeout in seconds (default 300).
.TP
.B CCODE_CA_FILE
Custom CA bundle for TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.B CCODE_ALLOW_HTTP
Set 1 to allow
.BR http://
API endpoints beyond loopback (plaintext, known risk). Loopback http
is always allowed; remote http is refused otherwise.
.TP
.B CCODE_WEB_FETCH_BLACKLIST
Comma-separated hostnames blacklisted for web_fetch (subdomains match).
.TP
.B CCODE_WEB_FETCH_RATE_LIMIT
Minimum seconds between web_fetch requests.
.TP
.B CCODE_WEB_FETCH_USER_AGENT
User-Agent for web_fetch.
.TP
.B CCODE_WEB_SEARCH_URL
URL template for web_search (must contain the
.I {query}
placeholder).
.SS Sessions
.TP
.B CCODE_SESSION_DIR
Session storage directory (default ~/.ccode/sessions).
.TP
.B CCODE_SESSION_AUTO_SAVE
Auto-save after each turn (default 1).
.TP
.B CCODE_SESSION_MAX_SIZE
Max session file size (default 10M).
.TP
.B CCODE_SESSION_KEEP_COUNT
Number of sessions to keep (default 10).
.SS Rendering
.TP
.B CCODE_MARKDOWN
Set 0 to disable markdown rendering.
.TP
.B CCODE_THINKING
Set 0 to disable thinking mode (enabled by default).
.TP
.B CCODE_THINKING_EFFORT
Thinking effort: low, medium, high, xhigh, max (default high).
Set to off, none or empty to omit the reasoning_effort field.
.TP
.B CCODE_CONTEXT_TOKENS
Approximate context window in tokens (default 1000000). Auto-compaction
triggers near 90% of it; 0 disables the token trigger.
.TP
.B CCODE_MAX_TURNS
Maximum assistant turns for one prompt (default 50; 0 means no limit).
Overridden by
.BR \-\-max-turns .
.SH LIMITS
Built-in (not configurable) resource bounds:
.TP
.B Command timeout
Each tool-spawned command is killed with its process group after 120
seconds of wall-clock time.
.TP
.B Command output
Stdout and stderr are each captured up to 64 KiB; excess is drained
(so the child never blocks) and reported as truncated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ccode/sessions/
Conversation session files (JSON v3).
.SH BUILD NOTES
.PP
Build with
.BR "make ccode-cli" .
HTTPS uses vendored mbedTLS by default; use
.B "make HTTP_ONLY=1"
for a plain-HTTP build. The retro i386 port (BasicLinux 3.5.1, libc5,
gcc 2.7.2.3 / egcs 1.1.2) builds with
.B "make RETRO=1 ccode-cli"
using the vendored PolarSSL 1.3.9 TLS backend, and the QEMU guest
pipeline is
.B "make retro-test"
(see docs/BASICLINUX.md).
